  "configuration_id": "config_029",
  "reason": "The evidence strongly identifies scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted (config_042, acc=0.7250) as the best configuration, and no untested configuration replicates that exact combination. For this final experiment, I select config_029 (scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) as the most logical remaining test: it retains the best RNA encoder (scvi_n200) and the preferred weighted fusion, while testing whether the slightly weaker image encoder (resnet50) and simpler aggregation (avgpool) can still approach the top result. Based on config_049 (resnet50+transformer+weighted, acc=0.713) and config_046 (imagenet_vit_l+avgpool+weighted, acc=0.706), I expect config_029 to land around 0.69–0.71, unlikely to surpass 0.7250 but informative. Expected relative cost is moderate (~4–5 GPU hours), as resnet50 is cheaper than ViT-L and avgpool is cheaper than transformer aggregation. Since this is the last experiment and the best result (0.7250) is already secured, this choice minimizes additional GPU cost while providing a final data point on the scvi_n200+weighted axis with a cheaper backbone."
}

